Your state of mind has no bearing on the structure you entered. The transaction is not a memory held by a witness who can forget, die, recant or be discredited; it is an event copied across a public record, fixed at the moment of execution and available to methods that did not exist when you acted. You can change addresses, fragment balances, cross jurisdictions, exchange assets, invent layers and wait for years, but none of those actions alters the first fact or destroys the path already written. They merely add material. Every movement becomes another timestamp, another relationship, another point at which separate records may eventually touch. You are not hiding the event from history. You are betting that history will never learn your name.

That wager has an asymmetry you cannot repair. Anyone examining the theft may fail a thousand times and return to the same evidence with better tools, broader datasets, compromised services, seized devices, cooperating intermediaries or one detail that acquires meaning only when placed beside another; you, by contrast, must remain correct every time, across every transfer, every conversion, every person, every machine and every year that remains to you. Spend the funds and you create contact. Move them and you create structure. Entrust them and you create a witness. Preserve them untouched and you protect wealth whose value is inseparable from the risk of ever using it. There is no final transaction after which certainty arrives, because you cannot inspect every database, control every counterparty, foresee every analytical advance or prove that the last useful trace has ceased to exist. The investigation is permitted to be wrong indefinitely. You are permitted to be wrong once.

Perhaps no one identifies you. That possibility changes nothing essential, because the life you selected contains no moment at which safety can be established as fact; there is only the continued absence of discovery, renewed each day and never guaranteed for the next. A knock may be meaningless, a frozen account may be routine, a delayed withdrawal may be technical, a familiar face may know nothing, but you will never possess the information required to prove which explanation is true until the distinction no longer belongs to you. The record does not tire, age or lose interest. It simply remains, complete enough to be reconsidered whenever the future acquires a sharper instrument. You did not take the money and disappear beyond the event. You placed yourself inside evidence that does not know your name yet, then gave time the rest of your life to discover it.
